.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-POOF 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-poof
.Nd clear keys and temporary secrets from a live session before walking away from it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A live session of the kldload image holds what was made or typed in it
\(em the certificate authority's key made for an install, WireGuard keys,
answers files with passwords in them \(em in memory, until it is powered
off.
.Nm
removes them, for when the machine is left running:
.Bl -enum
.It
blanks the private key of every WireGuard interface that is up;
.It
stops the SSH daemon;
.It
removes
.Pa /tmp/kldload-* ,
among them fetched answers files, and
.Pa /run/kldload ,
where secrets typed at the install screen are passed;
.It
shreds the certificate authority's root key,
.Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root/ca.key ;
.It
syncs, and drops the page cache.
.El
.Pp
It runs only in a live session, and must see one: the kernel command
line has
.Ql rd.live.image
or
.Ql root=live\&:
\(em every boot of the image, from a disk or the netboot server, has both
\(em or the live medium is at
.Pa /run/initramfs/live ;
and the install manifest does not mark the machine installed.
On an installed machine everything it does would be damage: the key it
shreds signs the machine's TLS certificates and its kernel modules.
.Pp
The web console's live mode runs it from a button.
It must run as root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description at the top of the script and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
For testing:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_POOF_CMDLINE
Read this file instead of
.Pa /proc/cmdline .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_POOF_LIVEDIR
Look for the live medium here instead of
.Pa /run/initramfs/live .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/poof.log
What it did.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/install-manifest.env
Marks an installed machine
.Pq Ql KLDLOAD_INSTALLED=1 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Done; anything it could not do is in the log above the summary.
.It 1
Not a live session, or a step failed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on 2026-09-30 in a container with a planted key, an answers file
and
.Pa /run/kldload ,
and a file standing in for a live kernel command line.
Its
.Pa /proc/sys
is read-only, hence the warning.
