.Ed
.Ss Where it refuses
The same container, standing in for an installed machine whose manifest
is missing, and then with the manifest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-poof
kldload-poof: this is not a live boot (no rd.live.image or root=live: on the kernel command line); refusing
# (exited 1)
# kldload-poof
kldload-poof only runs in live mode. Installed systems use ZFS encryption and boot environments.
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr shred 1 ,
.Xr kldload-ca 8 ,
.Xr wg 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-23 it looked for the authority's key in the wrong place,
reported that there was none, and left it.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: its only guard was the absence of the
installed marker, so an installed machine whose manifest was missing \(em
shown in a container \(em had its authority's key shredded; the step
named for SSH host keys removed none; and its last line said everything
had been cleared whatever had happened.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It does not overwrite memory that held a secret; it removes what holds
them now and drops the page cache.
Powering off is the complete scrub.
.Pp
The SSH host keys stay: they are the live image's, the same on every boot
of it.
